    "result_text": "I added `is_valid_email` to `lnbits/helpers.py` and switched the account validation to use it. I haven't run the tests, because the sandbox asked for approval on the pytest command and I haven't run it since.\n\n- **The helper:** `is_valid_email` does an anchored `re.fullmatch` on the whole string. I based it on the catalog's `validators.regex_match@v1` pattern and kept its `# pcat:` marker. `check_code` found no high-severity deviations. It reported two low ones, which are just the different regex literal for emails.\n- **Account validation:** `Account.validate_fields` in `lnbits/core/models/users.py` now calls `is_valid_email`.\n- **A missing function I found:** the repo already imports and calls `is_valid_email_address` in several places, including `auth_api.py`, `notifications.py` and `tests/unit/test_helpers.py`. `helpers.py` didn't define it, so those imports would have failed. I added `is_valid_email_address = is_valid_email` as an alias so they work again. If you'd rather rename those callers to `is_valid_email` and drop the alias, say so.\n\nTo run the tests: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_helpers.py`."
